---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/')?import.meta.env.BASE_URL:import.meta.env.BASE_URL+'/';
---
<SiteLayout title="Tear">
 <section class="tw-hero">
  <div class="tw-kicker">Fantasy tabletop role-playing game</div>
  <h1>TEAR</h1>
  <p>A fantasy tabletop role-playing game.</p>
  <div class="tw-actions">
   <a class="tw-btn tw-btn-primary" href={base+'create/species/'}>Create a Character</a>
   <a class="tw-btn tw-btn-outline" href={base+'world/'}>Explore the World</a>
  </div>
 </section>
 <section class="tw-content" id="about-tear">
  <p class="tw-eyebrow">Introduction</p>
  <h2>What is Tear?</h2>
  <p class="tw-lede">Tear is a classless fantasy role-playing game with flexible character development, tactical combat, and a world whose civilizations have been shaped by magic, divine rivalry, and history.</p>
  <div class="tw-card-grid" style="margin-top:33px">
   <a class="tw-card tw-card-link" href={base+'create/species/'}>
    <h3>Create a Character</h3><p>Begin with a species, then work through facets, attributes, skills, and equipment.</p>
    <span class="tw-card-label">Begin character creation →</span>
   </a>
   <a class="tw-card tw-card-link" href={base+'world/'}>
    <h3>Explore the World</h3><p>Take a guided tour or wander through Tear's library of lore.</p>
    <span class="tw-card-label">Discover Tear →</span>
   </a>
   <a class="tw-card tw-card-link" href={base+'rules/'}>
    <h3>Rules Reference</h3><p>Find the rules, spell compendium, equipment, and other game references.</p>
    <span class="tw-card-label">Browse the rules →</span>
   </a>
  </div>
 </section>
 <section class="tw-content tw-cta-section">
  <div>
   <h2>About the Project</h2>
   <p>Why I'm creating Tear, what I hope it can become, and how to support its development.</p>
  </div>
  <a class="tw-btn tw-btn-outline" href={base+'about/'}>About the Project →</a>
 </section>
</SiteLayout>